t $x=0$ along with their derivatives, as given in the table below.\n\n| $x$ | $f(x)$ | $g(x)$ | $f'(x)$ | $g'(x)$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $0$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ | $5$ |\n\nCan we calculate $\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}}{\\textrm{d}x}\\Big( f(x)g(x)\\Big )$ at $x=0?$\n\nUsing the product rule, we have\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}}{\\textrm{d}x}\\Big( f(x)g(x)\\Big) = f'(x)g(x)+f(x)g'(x).\n$$\n\nAt the point where $x=0,$ this gives\n\n$$\n\\left.\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}}{\\textrm{d}x}\\Big( f(x)g(x)\\Big) \\right|_{x=0}\t=\tf'(0)g(0)+f(0)g'(0).\n$$\n\nAll of these values are given in the table! So, substituting the values from the table into the formula, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(f(x)g(x))|}_{x=0} & ={f}^{′}(0)g(0)+f(0){g}^{′}(0) \\\\  & =4\\cdot 3+2\\cdot 5 \\\\  & =22.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186101942 #edb/ref 1065 2627 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186101942 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "9df0b4fa-df54-5f34-9bdc-3fc11befd2e8" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186101942 #edb/ref 1067 "Introduction" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186312286 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{5}{3}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186312286 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186312286 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "290f52b2-20e6-5905-988c-748802b627d7" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186314556 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186312286 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186314556 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186314556 #edb/ref 1077 "field-1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186314556 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186312286 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186314556 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "c222c8e2-34bd-53c8-8877-54fd0121599e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186315104 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186314556 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186315104 #edb/ref 1069 "q-341468" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186315104 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186315104 #edb/ref 1071 "The values of functions $h(t)$ and $z(t)$ and their derivatives at $t=4$ are given in the table below.\n\n| $t$ | $h(t)$ | $z(t)$ | ${h}^{′}(t)$ | ${z}^{′}(t)$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $4$ | $1$ | $-2$ | $3$ | $1$ |\n\nIf $f(t)=\\frac{2h(t)-5}{1-z(t)},$ compute ${f}^{′}(4).$ Do not round the answer.\n\n${f}^{′}(4)=$\n{{field-1}}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186315104 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "9a67f2b8-f03c-57a0-a261-901981830dca" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186315104 #edb/ref 1074 "The quotient rule states that\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\frac{u}{v})=\\frac{{u}^{′}v-u{v}^{′}}{{v}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nLet $u=2h(t)-5$ and $v=1-z(t).$ Differentiating each, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}t}=2{h}^{′}(t)\\,\\text{and}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t}=-{z}^{′}(t).\n$$\n\nSubstituting into the quotient rule gives\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(t)=\\frac{2{h}^{′}(t)(1-z(t))-(2h(t)-5)(-{z}^{′}(t))}{(1-z(t))^{2}}.\n$$\n\nAt $t=4,$ this gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(4) & =\\frac{2{h}^{′}(4)(1-z(4))-(2h(4)-5)(-{z}^{′}(4))}{(1-z(4))^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2(3)(1-(-2))-(2(1)-5)(-1)}{(1-(-2))^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2(3)(3)-(-3)(-1)}{(3)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{18-3}{9} \\\\  & =\\frac{15}{9} \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186339318 #edb/ref 1080 "-18" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186339318 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186339318 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "158ef797-3c95-5bcd-9718-13a56de44516" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186339615 #edb/ref 1080 "18" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186339615 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186339615 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "367510c1-9a7d-5efc-9a23-2d2dab4e5e4c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186339810 #edb/ref 1080 "9" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186339810 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186339810 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "4bce8f0b-d42b-5d9d-86f7-87536d507436" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [175921